  "bug_report_content": "Title: Caverphone encodes names starting and ending with \"mb\" incorrectly.\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nCaverphone encode names starting and ending with \"mb\" incorrectly.\n\nAccording to the spec:\n\"If the name ends with mb make it m2\".\n\nThis has been coded as:\n\"If the name _starts_ with mb make it m2\".\n\nComments:\n\n[Gary D. Gregory]: Forgot to check in this issue.",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.codec.language.Caverphone (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.codec.language.Caverphone (fixed)\n@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@\n         txt = txt.replaceAll(\"^gn\", \"2n\");\n \n         // End \n-        txt = txt.replaceAll(\"^mb\", \"m2\");\n+        txt = txt.replaceAll(\"mb$\", \"m2\");\n \n         // 4. Handle replacements\n         txt = txt.replaceAll(\"cq\", \"2q\");"
}